course: dictionary
lesson: 2664
title: Devote: giving your time and heart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To devote something means to give a lot of your time, effort or money to one thing. «Devote ten minutes to checking your work» tells you to spend those ten minutes on that one job and not on anything else.
explain: To devote yourself to someone or something means to care for it or work for it with your whole heart. The adjective devoted describes a loyal person or pet, like «devoted parents» who always stay by their children's side.
explain: Devote can also mean to set part of something aside for one purpose. «A page devoted to sport» means a whole page is kept for sport and not for other topics. The clue is in the words around it: the page is only for sport.
explain: «Monks and nuns live in communities devoted to prayer and service.» The clues are prayer and service, which are things you give your whole life to. So devoted to means given over completely to something.
fact: Devote is a verb: to devote means to give a lot of time, effort or money to one thing.
fact: Devoted is the adjective: a devoted fan supports a team with great loyalty.
fact: Useful phrases are devote time to, devote yourself to, and devoted to.
fact: «Devote» can also mean set aside for one use, as in «a page devoted to sport».
fact: A quick check: swap in give a lot of ... to. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «Ella devotes every Saturday morning to her piano practice.» What does devotes mean here? | Plays the piano badly on | Takes a break from | *Gives a lot of her time to | Forgets about
exercise: «The newspaper has a page devoted to sport.» What does devoted mean here? | Lost | Very loyal | *Set aside for one use | Thrown away
exercise: What does «a devoted fan» mean? | Bored by the game | *Loyal and caring | Very tall | Angry with the team
test: «Tom devoted his whole holiday to finishing his model ship.» What did Tom do? | Forgot about the model | Went on holiday to the sea | *Spent all his holiday on the model ship | Sold the ship
test: Which phrase means to work for something with your whole heart? | *Devote yourself to | Devote ten minutes to | A page devoted to | Devoted fan
exam: «The school asked parents to devote an hour a week to reading with their children.» What is the main meaning of devote here? | *Give a lot of time to one thing | Tell a secret | Hold tightly | Throw away
